NAME
       basename - strip directory and suffix from file names

SYNOPSIS
       basename NAME [SUFFIX]
       basename -a [-s SUFFIX] NAME...

DESCRIPTION
       Print NAME with any leading directory components removed, and a trailing
       SUFFIX if given.

OPTIONS
       -a
           support multiple arguments

       -s SUFFIX
           remove a trailing SUFFIX; implies -a

EXAMPLES
       basename /usr/bin/ls
       basename main.c .c

SEE ALSO
       dirname(1), realpath(1)
